      "writtenOn": "2026-11-24T12:51:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "you are injecting errors into fru-device. Of course if you inject errors there is going to be errors.\n\nSuch an error injection cannot establish that the corresponding error handling code can actually run in qemu or on a real hardware where the error is not injected like this.\n\nCan we inject the error instead at a boundary where it can actually occur ?\n\nIf the linux kernel is truly capable of generating the errors you are testing for then it should be possible to setup without injecting errors into userspace or drivers.",
